Final Answer:

### Sets and Indices

- Let $\mathcal{P}$ be the set of products, indexed by $i$ (from P1 to P111).
- Let $\mathcal{D}$ be the set of devices, indexed by $j$ (A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J).

### Parameters

From the CSVs:

- $p_i$: Unit profit of product $i$ (from unit_product_profits.csv)
- $a_{ji}$: Processing time required by product $i$ on device $j$ (from device_time.csv)
- $c_j$: Monthly operating capacity of device $j$ (from monthly_device_capacity.csv)

### Decision Variables

- $x_i \geq 0$: Production quantity of product $i$ (continuous, nonnegative)

### Mathematical Model

#### Objective

\[
\max \sum_{i \in \mathcal{P}} p_i x_i
\]

#### Constraints

For each device $j \in \mathcal{D}$:
\[
\sum_{i \in \mathcal{P}} a_{ji} x_i \leq c_j
\]

For all products $i \in \mathcal{P}$:
\[
x_i \geq 0
\]

---

### Complete Numerical Formulation

#### Sets

- $\mathcal{P} = \{\text{P1}, \text{P2}, \ldots, \text{P111}\}$
- $\mathcal{D} = \{\text{A}, \text{B}, \text{C}, \text{D}, \text{E}, \text{F}, \text{G}, \text{H}, \text{I}, \text{J}\}$

#### Parameters

From unit_product_profits.csv (partial for illustration; all 111 products included in the model):

